-- title:
--   Node cover identifies W₀ with the trace of 𝒪' (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 3$, $M'$ is a non-zero natural number not divisible by $q$, and $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of [`ValuationSubring.LiesOverPrime`](def/FLTPrelim_Ramification.html#L16), i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A` denotes its residue field. The finset $W$ of places of $\kappa \subseteq$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (the field generated over $\kappa$ by the $q$-expansions $j$ and $j(q\cdot)$, here by `jqModC` and `jqNModC`) is required by `hW` to have as its members exactly the elements of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, that is the places $w$ that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at the generator `jGeomGen κ M'` lies in `ssJSet q κ`; one such place $s \in W$ is fixed.
--
--   The inclusion `hle` asserts $\bar F_{M'} :=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\le$ `fieldBar q M'`, where $\bar F_{M'}$ is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` $= \mathbb Q(q\text{-expansions }j(d\cdot),\, d \mid M')$ inside Laurent series, and `fieldBar q M'` is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the $X_H$-function field of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup `levelH q M'` $= \ker((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times)$. The datum $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction A`-structure for $\bar F_{M'}$ with values in `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\bar F_{M'}$ whose constants are exactly $A$, a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` with kernel the maximal ideal, a map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places compatible with reduction of constants, degrees and divisor push-forward, and the scaling clause `exists_smul_mem`. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ lies in $\bar F_{M'}$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   On the side of constants: $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ has image in $A$; the ring $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, and `hκ` requires every element of $A$ to be congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$. An element $\zeta$ of `Idx q` (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) is fixed; the name is re-bound by the quantifiers below. Finally $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $K_b = \bot$, $A_b$ is a valuation subring of $K_b$ whose members are exactly the elements of $K_b$ lying in $A$, and $\varpi_b \in A_b$ is a non-zero generator of the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   The valuation subring $\mathcal O'$ of `fieldBar q M'` satisfies three hypotheses. `hO'_A`: for $x \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$, the image of $x$ lies in $\mathcal O'$ if and only if $x \in A$. `hO'_over`: for every $f \in \bar F_{M'}$ lying in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ such that $f$ has non-negative order at every place $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q} \subseteq \bar F_{M'}$ at which the coefficientwise image of `jq` has non-negative order, and such that $R_0.\mathrm{residue}\,f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $\mathcal O'$, and for every $a \in A$ with $\mathrm{residue}_A(a) = s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}\,f)$ the difference of the image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in $\mathcal O'$ and in its maximal ideal. `hO'_fix`: for every $\zeta' \in$ `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \subseteq \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, the comap of $\mathcal O'$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` is $\mathcal O'$.
--
--   With `fieldBar q M'` regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is then universally quantified over the following data. First, an intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0 \subseteq$ `fieldBar q M'` stable under all `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. Second, a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that: for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $W_0$; $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal; and ($W_0$ lies over $s$) for every $g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficient-embedded image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, has non-negative order at every place where the image of `jq` does, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ and $\mathrm{residue}_A(c) = s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue})$ of that element, the difference of the image of $g$ and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal.
--
--   Third, a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` together with an $A_b$-algebra structure `alg` on $B$ subject to: compatibility, namely for $a \in A_b$ the image in `fieldBar q M'` of $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,a$ is the image of $a$ viewed in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and there in $W_0$; $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,\varpi_b$ is a prime element of $B$; $W_0$ is the corresponding localisation, i.e. $f \in F_0$ lies in $W_0$ exactly when $f h = g$ in `fieldBar q M'` for some $g, h \in B$ with $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,\varpi_b \nmid h$; $B$ is stable under all `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and a Drinfeld presentation of the special fibre: for every $\mathrm{GaloisField}(q,2)$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GaloisField}(q,2)$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field in the Drinfeld function field $\mathrm{Frac}(\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa)$ of the group generated by the actions of the elements $(1,\zeta)$, $\zeta \in C_s$) such that: $\#C_s = 2\,\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, where `placeWidthChar` is `jWidthChar q` of the value of the place at `jGeomGen` divided by `placeRamificationJ M'` of the place, and for $q = 3$ the numerator is $6$ at $j = 0$ and $1$ otherwise; $\ker \rho$ is the ideal generated by $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,\varpi_b$; on $A_b$ the map $\rho$ is reduction $A \to \kappa$ followed by the structure map of `quotField`; every element of `quotField q κ Cs` is a ratio $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $g,h \in B$ and $\rho(h) \neq 0$; the range of $\rho$ consists exactly of those elements whose image in the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of `CoordRing q κ`; and $\rho$ is equivariant, in the sense that for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) and $f \in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` $f \in B$, the image of the latter under $\rho$ equals [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at that group element applied to the image of $\rho(f)$ in the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   Fourth, a finset `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$ with: cardinality $q+1$; equivariance, namely for every $\zeta$, every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $O_1 \in$ `nodes` there is $O_2 \in$ `nodes` such that for all $f \in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` $f \in F_0$ one has $f \in O_1$ if and only if that image lies in $O_2$; transitivity, namely for every $\zeta$ and all $O_1, O_2 \in$ `nodes` there is $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ realising the same equivalence; separation, namely for distinct $O_1, O_2 \in$ `nodes` there is $f \in F_0$ belonging to both which is a non-unit of $O_1$ and a unit of $O_2$; and a covering clause, namely every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ whose constants on $k_0$ are $A$ and which lies over $s$ in exactly the sense stated above for $W_0$ either contains $B$ (every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and there in $V$) or dominates a node: there is $O \in$ `nodes` with every $f \in O$ lying in $V$ and with every non-unit of $O$ lying in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   Under all of this, the conclusion is the single equivalence: for every $f \in F_0$, $f \in W_0$ if and only if the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $\mathcal O'$; that is, $W_0$ is the trace of $\mathcal O'$ on $F_0$.
--
--   This is the $q = 3$ instance, at an auxiliary level rigidified by a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the identification of the valuation ring attached to a supersingular point of $X_0(M')$ in characteristic $q$ with the ring cut out on a $k_0$-rational form by an affine chart whose special fibre is a Drinfeld curve $C_s$-quotient, the $q+1$ node rings accounting for the components meeting the supersingular annulus. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_nodeChart_point_specializes_iff_adicCompletion_stalk_of_normalModel_gen_j_local_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_nodeChart_point_specializes_iff_adicCompletion_stalk_of_normalModel_gen_j_local_of_eq_three_of_dvd) and by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_drinfeldRing_iff_localization_formallySmooth_card_le_descent_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_drinfeldRing_iff_localization_formallySmooth_card_le_descent_of_eq_three_of_dvd) in the construction of the semistable model at level $q^2M'$.
